---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import StatusNotice from '../components/StatusNotice.astro';
import runtimes from '../data/runtimes.json';
---
<Site title="Bootstrap status" description="Current Logifos engine and runtime status: unreleased scaffolds, with rendering unavailable." page="home">
  <section class="opening" aria-labelledby="title">
    <p class="kicker">Math formula rendering / project status</p>
    <h1 id="title">The foundation<br />comes first.</h1>
    <p class="introduction">Logifos is being built as a Rust math formula engine with Ruby, TypeScript, and Python runtimes.</p>
    <StatusNotice />
  </section>
  <section id="status" aria-labelledby="status-title">
    <h2 id="status-title">Current engine and runtimes</h2>
    <p>Bootstrap preparation does not qualify a rendering runtime.</p>
    <dl class="runtime-list">
      {runtimes.map((runtime) => (
        <div data-component={runtime.id} data-status="scaffold">
          <dt>{runtime.name}<a href={`https://github.com/logifos/${runtime.repository}`}>{runtime.package}</a></dt>
          <dd><span class="status-label">Scaffold</span><p>No released rendering version; rendering is unavailable.</p></dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>
    <p><a href="/status.html#runtime-matrix">Read the runtime and version matrix →</a></p>
  </section>
  <section class="next-steps" aria-labelledby="next-title">
    <h2 id="next-title">Planned next steps</h2>
    <p>The planned sequence starts with MathML, followed by layout and SVG. Ruby and PNG qualification precede TypeScript and Python delivery. LaTeX follows MathML; AsciiMath comes last. These are planned gates, not completed capabilities.</p>
    <p>Ruby and TypeScript are intended to launch together after both qualify. Python follows.</p>
    <a href="/architecture.html">Explore the planned architecture →</a>
  </section>
</Site>
